076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534568 17592186045417 true] [17592186425974 1077 "selection" 13194139534568 17592186045417 true] [17592186425974 1078 #edb/ref 17592186425965 13194139534568 17592186045417 true] [17592186425974 1079 #uuid "97aeada7-12fc-5a6f-b3b8-8465455bada0" 13194139534568 17592186045417 true] [17592186425975 1075 #edb/ref 17592186425956 13194139534568 17592186045417 true] [17592186425975 1075 #edb/ref 17592186425957 13194139534568 17592186045417 true] [17592186425975 1075 #edb/ref 17592186425959 13194139534568 17592186045417 true] [17592186425975 1075 #edb/ref 17592186425960 13194139534568 17592186045417 true] [17592186425975 1075 #edb/ref 17592186425972 13194139534568 17592186045417 true] [17592186425975 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534568 17592186045417 true] [17592186425975 1077 "selection" 13194139534568 17592186045417 true] [17592186425975 1078 #edb/ref 17592186425959 13194139534568 17592186045417 true] [17592186425975 1079 #uuid "c5aa0841-040f-5aec-85ca-fd3f64c07a51" 13194139534568 17592186045417 true] [17592186425976 1075 #edb/ref 17592186425953 13194139534568 17592186045417 true] [17592186425976 1075 #edb/ref 17592186425954 13194139534568 17592186045417 true] [17592186425976 1075 #edb/ref 17592186425961 13194139534568 17592186045417 true] [17592186425976 1075 #edb/ref 17592186425967 13194139534568 17592186045417 true] [17592186425976 1075 #edb/ref 17592186425968 13194139534568 17592186045417 true] [17592186425976 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534568 17592186045417 true] [17592186425976 1077 "selection" 13194139534568 17592186045417 true] [17592186425976 1078 #edb/ref 17592186425954 13194139534568 17592186045417 true] [17592186425976 1079 #uuid "fd267c3d-501f-5503-9b5e-c946c034c0d4" 13194139534568 17592186045417 true] [17592186425977 1068 #edb/ref 17592186425975 13194139534568 17592186045417 true] [17592186425977 1069 "q-175372" 13194139534568 17592186045417 true] [17592186425977 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534568 17592186045417 true] [17592186425977 1071 "Find the truth set of the following predicate:\n\n$\\,$ $P(x):$ ${x}^{2}<9$\n\nwhere the universal set is $R.$" 13194139534568 17592186045417 true] [17592186425977 1072 #uuid "0237c8ad-eb27-521a-9b96-cd671ad62b96" 13194139534568 17592186045417 true] [17592186425977 1074 "The *truth set* of a predicate $P(x)$ is the set of elements in its universal set $U$ such that substituting these elements for the variable makes the predicate a true statement:\n\n$$\nT=\\{x\\in U\\,|\\,P(x)\\}\n$$\n\nThe universal set for our predicate is $U=R.$\n\nWe need to find $x\\in U$ such that the following is true:\n\n$\\,$ ${x}^{2}<9$\n\nTaking the square root of both sides of the inequality, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & <9 \\\\ \\sqrt{{x}^{2}} & <\\sqrt{9} \\\\ |x| & <3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the definition of absolute value, we must have\n\n$$\n-3\\text{ }<x<3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the truth set of our predicate is $T=(-3,3).$" 13194139534568 17592186045417 true] [17592186425978 1068 #edb/ref 17592186425974 13194139534568 17592186045417 true] [17592186425978 1069 "q-175361" 13194139534568 17592186045417 true] [17592186425978 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534568 17592186045417 true] [17592186425978 1071 "Find the truth set of the following predicate:\n\n$\\,$ $P(x):$ $5x+2>22,$\n\nwhere the universal set is $R.$" 13194139534568 17592186045417 true] [17592186425978 1072 #uuid "10a98313-2524-5ce8-a6f0-176526143e93" 13194139534568 17592186045417 true] [17592186425978 1074 "The *truth set* of a predicate $P(x)$ is the set of elements in its universal set $U$ such that substituting these elements for the variable makes the predicate a true statement:\n\n$$\nT=\\{x\\in U\\,|\\,P(x)\\}\n$$\n\nWe need to find $x\\in U$ such that the following is true:\n\n$\\,$ $5x+2>22$\n\nThe universal set for our predicate is $U=R.$\n\nNow, we need to solve the above inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x+2>22 \\\\ 5x>20 \\\\ x>4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the truth set of our predicate is\n\n$$\nT=(4,\\infty ).\n$$" 13194139534568 17592186045417 true] [17592186425979 1068 #edb/ref 17592186425976 13194139534568 17592186045417 true] [17592186425979 1069 "q-175390" 13194139534568 17592186045417 true] [17592186425979 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534568 17592186045417 true] [17592186425979 1071 "Consider the following predicate:\n\n$\\,$ $P(x,y):$ $x+y\\le 0,$\n\nwhere the universal set is ${R}^{2}.$ Which of the following shaded regions represents the truth set of the predicate?" 13194139534568 17592186045417 true] [17592186425979 1072 #uuid "713f4e9c-4d96-5c9b-be62-26529dd25eb1" 13194139534568 17592186045417 true] [17592186425979 1074 "The *truth set* of a predicate $P({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})$ is the set of $n$-tuples in its universal set $U={U}_{1}\\times {U}_{2}\\times ⋯\\times {U}_{n}$ such that substituting these tuples for the variables makes the predicate a true statement:\n\n$$\nT=\\{({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\in U\\,|\\,P({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\}\n$$\n\nThe universal set for our predicate is $U={R}^{2}.$\n\nWe need to find $(x,y)\\in U$ such that the following is true:\n\n$\\,$ $x+y\\le 0$\n\nNow, we convert the inequality into the slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+y & \\le 0 \\\\ y & \\le -x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, let's sketch the truth set $T$ of $P(x,y):$\n\n![](images/1e/1e8f03a8b229a8b2e46af33c700dec57a8abed693a58c75b6312e2ae5a6856c1.png)" 13194139534568 17592186045417 true] [17592186425980 1068 #edb/ref 17592186425973 13194139534568 17592186045417 true] [17592186425980 1069 "q-175366" 13194139534568 17592186045417 true] [17592186425980 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534568 17592186045417 true] [17592186425980 1071 "Which of the following are mathematical predicates?\n\nI. $P(y):$ ${y}^{2}-1=8$\n\nII. $Q(a,b):$ ${a}^{2}+{b}^{2}$\n\nIII. $R(x,y):$ $\\frac{x}{y}\\in N\\cap Q$" 13194139534568 17592186045417 true] [17592186425980 1072 #uuid "86866e7c-73c9-5409-8743-b71ad4d3cbe4" 13194139534568 17592186045417 true] [17592186425980 1074 "A *predicate* of the variables ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ is a sentence that contains the variables defined on some *universal set*, and has the property that when we substitute concrete values for all the variables into the predicate, the result becomes a statement that is either true or false.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our options. \n\n- Option I is a predicate of one variable. Substituting a concrete value for $y$ into the sentence, we get a statement that is either true or false.\n\n- Option II is *not* a predicate. Substituting a concrete pair of values $(a,b)$ into the sentence, we do not get a statement that is either true or false.\n\n- Option III is a predicate of two variables. Substituting a concrete pair of values $(x,y)$ into the sentence, we get a statement that is either true or false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" 13194139534568 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-13edba04-7016-55b3-998a-0c1a02b2d307" 17592186425953 "answer-1a94059a-c75b-54d5-86b6-d7a3d7e98d53" 17592186425954 "answer-3663dea6-8f8d-54bc-864f-6cdf19f19c88" 17592186425955 "answer-3cde1ebc-e432-58be-aec4-61a0a888f799" 17592186425956 "answer-4ff057a1-4c2b-565a-83cd-56aa95d66144" 17592186425957 "answer-58b7a612-07c6-5679-8d42-d625deb5e970" 17592186425958 "answer-5d21df02-6b8d-5e86-a2f9-f452aee05936" 17592186425959 "answer-61c53b8b-e43b-5a05-9fb3-abadd0684739" 17592186425960 "answer-722f7e6a-002b-544e-97b2-40986c6598f4" 17592186425961 "answer-89c42d97-1ffe-532c-88ad-c4354d4cacc9" 17592186425962 "answer-8aae07b3-7050-585d-9ab2-29e7b26a079e" 17592186425963 "answer-9267effc-1c42-535d-b1dc-8a9d238e9d00" 17592186425964 "answer-d143d075-6812-5d2c-bd24-7bc7894f07b7" 17592186425965 "answer-d4423da0-b4c9-5f1f-83a8-6ee54f9efc80" 17592186425966 "answer-d49d4e89-b150-588d-b862-2ff8d4d1e8e1" 17592186425967 "answer-d882ad0a-e078-5ea7-908f-611bb3476cea" 17592186425968 "an